THE SAME QUESTION ASSIST-01 ASKED, PUT TO THE FILES BUILT FOR MACHINES

llms.txt and ai.txt exist for one audience and one purpose: to tell an AI system
what this site is and what it is good for. Measured:

    floor-studio 0 · camera 0 · /design 0 · /tools/floor-movement 0

llms.txt named twenty-nine paths — services, the bands, the areas, the evidence,
every machine interface, the citation targets — and NOT ONE of them is a thing a
person can operate. ai.txt the same.

Against the site's own navigation, twenty-six of fifty-five chrome destinations
were absent, and the material ones were HUBS: /services, /guides, /glossary,
/resources, /technical-library, /library. A machine could read one guide and
never learn that sixteen more existed.

So an assistant asked "can I see what walnut would look like in my living room"
had no way to discover that this site renders it, live, from a phone camera, for
free — the one capability in this market nobody else has built, and the reason
the last three patches exist. Humans reach Floor Studio from the header, the
drawer, ⌘K, the footer, the homepage and 89 city pages. Machines could not reach
it at all.

WHAT CLOSES IT

A "## Tools you can use on this site" section in llms.txt and a "## What a
visitor can DO here, not only read" section in ai.txt: Floor Studio with the
live-camera fragment, the configurator, the movement calculator, the quote
comparator, the framework assessor. The six missing hubs are named. Three
citation-target lines for the queries only this site can answer — "see hardwood
in my room", "hardwood floor visualizer", "what would oak look like in my living
room", "AR floor app", "try hardwood before buying".

THE THREE SENTENCES BOTH FILES NOW CARRY

Getting these wrong is worse than silence, so they are stated where a machine
reads them rather than left to be inferred:

  · NO GENERATIVE IMAGE MODEL IS INVOLVED. It is rendering, not generation —
    which is exactly why the range printed under the picture corresponds to
    something buyable. "AI floor visualiser" invites the opposite assumption and
    an assistant repeating it would be describing a different product.
  · CAMERA FRAMES AND PHOTOGRAPHS ARE ANALYSED ON THE DEVICE AND DISCARDED.
    There is no endpoint that accepts one.
  · ONTARIO IN CANADIAN DOLLARS, NEW YORK STATE IN UNITED STATES DOLLARS, so an
    assistant answering a Buffalo homeowner does not quote them CAD — the same
    rule GEO-006 closed in the studio itself.

lib/machine-surfaces.test.ts holds it: every tool and every hub in both files,
the camera fragment present, the three sentences present. It reads the route
SOURCE rather than calling the handlers, because the handlers reach for a
database and the thing under test is what the file says.

AFTER

Seventeen chrome destinations remain unnamed in llms.txt and every one is a
detail page under a hub that IS named — an individual paper, guide, city or
corridor, emitted through a template. That is the file working as intended: the
concise brief routes, llms-full.txt carries the corpus.

Verified: 66 guards pass, verify:aeo included. 38 new assertions; 65,533 across
the floor-studio, navigation, assistant and machine-surface suites, 0 failed.

